if (irq < 0) {
    DPU_ERROR("failed to get irq: %d\n", irq);
    return irq;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code incorrectly checks if the return value of `irq_of_parse_and_map()` is less than zero to determine if an error has occurred. Since this function returns 0 on failure and does not return negative values, the condition will never be true, leading to the failure case not being handled properly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!irq) {
    DPU_ERROR("failed to get irq\n");
    return -EINVAL;
}
```
Reason:
The fix changes the condition to check if `irq` is equal to 0 instead of checking if it is less than zero. This correctly identifies the failure case when `irq_of_parse_and_map()` fails, allowing the error to be handled appropriately by logging the error and returning a negative error code (`-EINVAL`).

